{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/978744-pack-members","id":978744,"title":"Pack Members","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T18:04:11-07:00","id":978744,"title":"Pack Members","content":"Hi folks, I'm looking to start a game of Werewolf soon and I was wondering how you guys have handled the additional pack members 2E bakes in. I've got no problem with it conceptionally, I would just like to hear some examples of how you guys have integrated them into the game. Do you treat them as freebie Allies/Contacts, do they meet up with the player's characters regularly, do they join in on combat etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:22:55-07:00","id":978753,"title":"","content":"Ours met up with our characters regularly. They wouldn't join in on hunts but our pack was purists and my character, one of the hunt ritemasters, insisted on hunts ending with death.<br /> <br /> Some acted as free contacts and allies, or allies with contacts. We were able to get a lot of information, acting as plot hooks, through them. Some would be sort of like the totem, links to the supernatural world, them having been in the area longer than us, even if they only had their Tells. Our 'high priestess,' was basically the mortal leader of a cult, with her Tell allowing the patron spirit of it to act through her and take care of all the magical parts of things. Others would act like 'background' NPCs, I guess, family and friends who might be able to drive somewhere to pick you up in the middle of the night without asking too many questions. Those didn't all know what we were about.<br /> <br /> I'd be tempted to say the wolf-blooded were the ones we kept more in on things, while the humans were the ones we were just friends with, but there were a couple wolf-blooded we didn't really let in on the secret during our game. To be fair, it was mostly because due to their circumstances, a death in the family and having been under a Vinculum, we weren't entirely sure they would be able to deal with the revelation. At least one of our human numbers knew about everything, or at least saw a bit of everything, but she was sort of a reluctant member of the pack to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-29-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}